A bind takes the place's own virtual time and not the latest of it and its new units'.
A thread that ran ahead of its units would shed it by giving them to another thread of its process, and the other run at once;
no bind puts back a unit's time.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a call put a unit's virtual time back
Witness: fuzz units-keep-vtime

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -644,9 +644,6 @@ void sched_bind(struct place *p, uint32_t first, uint32_t count, uint8_t rights,
     for (uint32_t i = 0; i < count; i++) {
         LOOP_BOUND(TIME_UNITS);
         unit_place[first + i] = v2p(p);
-        if (unit_vt[first + i] > p->vt) {
-            p->vt = unit_vt[first + i];
-        }
     }
     lender_settle(place_thread(p));
 }
